    "notes": {
        "23858c64-d3fa-46bc-abac-b34dbf8f1fa2": {
            "x": 64,
            "y": 576,
            "width": 736,
            "height": 320,
            "content": "## \u26a0\ufe0f Test data assumption\n\nThese flows work against the **permanently open pull request [`apx-vero/appmixer-test` #5](https://github.com/apx-vero/appmixer-test/pull/5)** (\"Exercise the new review components\", head `review-components-smoke`).\n\nIt adds a single file `review-components-smoke.txt` with five lines, so lines 1-5 are all part of the diff and can be commented on with side `RIGHT`. Two review threads created by hand live on it \u2014 they are what List Review Threads / List Reviews read.\n\n**If the pull request is missing or closed, every flow here fails or times out.** Recreate it:\n\n1. `git checkout -b review-components-smoke master` in `apx-vero/appmixer-test`\n2. add `review-components-smoke.txt` containing the lines `line one` \u2026 `line five`, commit and push\n3. open a pull request against `master` and leave it OPEN\n4. post one inline review comment on line 3 and reply to it once (that is the thread the resolve/unresolve steps operate on)\n\n## \u23f2\ufe0f Timing and leftovers\n\nThe `Wait 1m` must stay - the trigger records its polling window when the flow starts and only reports reviews submitted after that. GitHub cannot delete a submitted review, so each run leaves one more COMMENT review on the pull request; that is harmless and there is nothing to clean up. An APPROVE review is deliberately NOT used: GitHub refuses to let an account approve its own pull request.\n"
        }
    }
